course: dictionary
lesson: 565
title: Family words: aunt
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An aunt is a family word. Your aunt is the sister of your mum or your dad, and she can also be the wife of your uncle. «Auntie» is a friendly word for an aunt, and it is also used for an older woman friend of the family, even when she is not related to you.
explain: Look at the words around a new family word. «A boy said he was too tired to visit his great-aunt, who had been looking forward to it.» The word great-aunt tells you she is a special kind of aunt, and the sentence shows she is someone the family cares about, because she had been looking forward to the visit.
explain: Other sentences can give you clues too. «Cousins are the children of your aunts and uncles.» If you know who your cousins are, you can work out who your aunts are: an aunt is the parent of one of your cousins, or the sister of one of your parents.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put «the sister of your mum or dad» in place of aunt and see if it still makes sense. If it does, you have understood the word.
fact: An aunt is the sister of your mother or father.
fact: An aunt is also the wife of your uncle.
fact: «Auntie» is a friendly word for an aunt, or for an older woman friend of the family.
fact: «Great-aunt» means your parent's aunt.
fact: Cousins are the children of your aunts and uncles, and families spread out, so some cousins only meet at weddings and funerals.
exercise: «Cousins are the children of your aunts and uncles.» Who are your cousins? | *The children of your aunts and uncles | Your best friends at school | Your grandparents | Your parents' brothers
exercise: «A boy said he was too tired to visit his great-aunt.» Who is a great-aunt? | *Your parent's aunt | Your cousin | The wife of your dad's brother's dog | A friend of your teacher
exercise: Mia says «Auntie» is a word only for babies. Is she right? | *No, it is a friendly word for an aunt or an older woman friend of the family | Yes, it means a sister who is older than you | No, it means a grandmother | Yes, it is only for babies
test: Which person is your aunt? | Your mum's daughter | *The sister of your mum or dad | Your dad's son | Your brother's friend
test: Which word is a friendly name for an aunt? | Grandad | Cousin | *Auntie | Nephew
exam: Ali says «Auntie» means a cousin. Is Ali right? | Yes, it means your mum's mum | No, it means a family dog | *Yes, it means the child of your aunt | No, auntie is a friendly word for an aunt or an older woman friend of the family
